  m_text: '

    First you need to create your Character object.


    An object
    is a collection of data types. Some important data types are:


    <b>char:</b>
    A char is a character. It can be a letter, number or any character on your keyboard.
    Eg. ''a''


    <b>string:</b> A string is a collection of characters. It can
    be a word, sentence, paragraph etc. Eg. "Hello, world!"


    <b>integer:</b>
    An integer is a natural number, whole number or number without a decimal place.
    Eg. 7


    <b>float:</b> A float is a number with a fixed number of decimal
    places. Eg. 1.05


    <b>double:</b> A double is a number with a lot more decimal
    places than a float. Eg. 0.5789684523214786


    <b>boolean:</b> A boolean can
    have two possible values: true or false


    Finish creating the Character object
    to create your character.'
